   "short": false,
   "hook": "Jarasum Jazz Festival: jazz on Turtle Island",
   "name_chips": true,
   "lines": [
    {
     "who": "anchor",
     "text": "Time for a different kind of news. Two festivals happening right now in Korea. One has jazz on an island. The other has movies in Korea's second-largest city.",
     "audio": "audio/v1/ep05_001.mp3",
     "shot": "k_screen",
     "cam_id": "screen_anchor",
     "push": false,
     "screen": "two_fest"
    },
    {
     "who": "panel",
     "text": "I'm in. Both. Where do I sign?",
     "audio": "audio/v1/ep05_002.mp3",
     "shot": "cam",
     "cam": [
      960,
      500,
      1.1
     ],
     "ease": 0.14,
     "cam_id": "two",
     "push": false
    },
    {
     "who": "anchor",
     "text": "To help us plan, our travel expert, Professor Indoor.",
     "audio": "audio/v1/ep05_003.mp3",
     "shot": "cam",
     "cam": [
      960,
      500,
      1.1
     ],
     "ease": 0.14,
     "cam_id": "two",
     "push": false
    },
    {
     "who": "guest",
     "text": "I've been to both.",
     "audio": "audio/v1/ep05_004.mp3",
     "shot": "cam",
     "cam": [
      2560,
      470,
      1.3
     ],
     "ease": 0.12,
     "cam_id": "guest",
     "push": false
    },
    {
     "who": "anchor",
     "text": "Physically?",
     "audio": "audio/v1/ep05_005.mp3",
     "shot": "cam",
     "cam": [
      960,
      500,
      1.1
     ],
     "ease": 0.14,
     "cam_id": "two",
     "push": false
    },
    {
     "who": "guest",
     "text": "...Emotionally. I watched a lot of street view.",
     "audio": "audio/v1/ep05_006.mp3",
     "shot": "cam",
     "cam": [
      2560,
      470,
      1.3
     ],
     "ease": 0.12,
     "cam_id": "guest",
     "push": false
    },
    {
     "who": "anchor",
     "text": "We'll take it. Let's start with the jazz.",
     "audio": "audio/v1/ep05_007.mp3",
     "shot": "cam",
     "cam": [
      960,
      500,
      1.1
     ],
     "ease": 0.14,
     "cam_id": "two",
     "push": false
    },
    {
     "who": "anchor",
     "text": "The Jarasum International Jazz Festival. October ninth to eleventh, in Gapyeong, about seventy kilometers northeast of Seoul.",
     "audio": "audio/v1/ep05_008.mp3",
     "shot": "k_screen",
     "cam_id": "screen_anchor",
     "push": false,
     "screen": "jarasum_autumn"
    },
    {
     "who": "panel",
     "text": "Jarasum. That sounds like a dinosaur.",
     "audio": "audio/v1/ep05_009.mp3",
     "shot": "k_screen",
     "cam_id": "screen_panel",
     "side": "left",
     "push": false,
     "screen": "turtle"
    },
    {
     "who": "anchor",
     "text": "It's not a dinosaur. \"Jarasum\" means \"terrapin island.\" A terrapin is a kind of turtle.",
     "audio": "audio/v1/ep05_010.mp3",
     "shot": "k_screen",
     "cam_id": "screen_anchor",
     "push": false,
     "screen": "turtle"
    },
    {
     "who": "panel",
     "text": "A jazz festival on Turtle Island. So the tempo is... slow?",
     "audio": "audio/v1/ep05_011.mp3",
     "shot": "k_screen",
     "cam_id": "screen_panel",
     "side": "left",
     "push": false,
     "screen": "turtle"
    },
    {
     "who": "anchor",
     "text": "Technically, it's a group of four small islands in the Bukhan River: East, West, Middle, and South.",
     "audio": "audio/v1/ep05_012.mp3",
     "shot": "k_screen",
     "cam_id": "screen_anchor",
     "push": false,
     "screen": "jarasum_autumn"
    },
    {
     "who": "panel",
     "text": "East, West, Middle, South. Whoever named those islands did it on a lunch break.",
     "audio": "audio/v1/ep05_013.mp3",
     "shot": "k_screen",
     "cam_id": "screen_panel",
     "side": "left",
     "push": false,
     "screen": "jarasum_autumn"
    },
    {
     "who": "anchor",
     "text": "It started in two thousand four, with thirty teams of musicians from twelve countries.",
     "audio": "audio/v1/ep05_014.mp3",
     "shot": "k_screen",
     "cam_id": "screen_anchor",
     "push": false,
     "screen": "y2004"
    },
    {
     "who": "panel",
     "text": "Two thousand four. Back then my biggest problem was burning a CD without it skipping.",
     "audio": "audio/v1/ep05_015.mp3",
     "shot": "k_screen",
     "cam_id": "screen_panel",
     "side": "left",
     "push": false,
     "screen": "y2004"
    },
    {
     "who": "anchor",
     "text": "This year is the twenty-third edition. And the government has noticed: it was named a \"Representative Festival of Korea\" in twenty sixteen and again in twenty eighteen.",
     "audio": "audio/v1/ep05_016.mp3",
     "shot": "k_screen",
     "cam_id": "screen_anchor",
     "push": false,
     "screen": "jarasum_time"
    },
    {
     "who": "panel",
     "text": "So it got a gold star. Twice.",
     "audio": "audio/v1/ep05_017.mp3",
     "shot": "k_screen",
     "cam_id": "screen_panel",
     "side": "left",
     "push": false,
     "screen": "jarasum_time"
    },
    {
     "who": "anchor",
     "text": "In twenty twenty-three, it joined the Europe Jazz Network. And each year it puts one country in the spotlight. Poland, then Hungary last year.",
     "audio": "audio/v1/ep05_018.mp3",
     "shot": "k_screen",
     "cam_id": "screen_anchor",
     "push": false,
     "screen": "jarasum_time"
    },
    {
     "who": "panel",
     "text": "Poland, Hungary... and this year?",
     "audio": "audio/v1/ep05_019.mp3",
     "shot": "k_screen",
     "cam_id": "screen_panel",
     "side": "left",
     "push": false,
     "screen": "france_flag"
    },
    {
     "who": "anchor",
     "text": "France. It marks one hundred forty years of diplomatic ties between Korea and France.",
     "audio": "audio/v1/ep05_020.mp3",
     "shot": "k_screen",
     "cam_id": "screen_anchor",
     "push": false,
     "screen": "france_flag"
    },
    {
     "who": "panel",
     "text": "One hundred forty years. I can't keep a houseplant alive for one.",
     "audio": "audio/v1/ep05_021.mp3",
     "shot": "k_screen",
     "cam_id": "screen_panel",
     "side": "left",
     "push": false,
     "screen": "france_flag"
    },
    {
     "who": "anchor",
     "text": "The poster is by a French illustrator, Agathe Briot. Two dancers, a lot of color.",
     "audio": "audio/v1/ep05_022.mp3",
     "shot": "k_screen",
     "cam_id": "screen_anchor",
     "push": false,
     "screen": "jarasum_poster"
    },
    {
     "who": "panel",
     "text": "Okay, nice poster. But who's actually playing?",
     "audio": "audio/v1/ep05_023.mp3",
     "shot": "k_screen",
     "cam_id": "screen_panel",
     "side": "left",
     "push": false,
     "screen": "jarasum_poster"
    },
    {
     "who": "anchor",
     "text": "Headliners include drummer Nate Smith. He won two Grammys this year, and this is his first time back at Jarasum in seventeen years.",
     "audio": "audio/v1/ep05_024.mp3",
     "shot": "k_screen",
     "cam_id": "screen_anchor",
     "push": false,
     "screen": [
      "nate_smith",
      "years17"
     ]
    },
    {
     "who": "panel",
     "text": "Seventeen years. That's the longest rest in music history.",
     "audio": "audio/v1/ep05_025.mp3",
     "shot": "k_screen",
     "cam_id": "screen_panel",
     "side": "left",
     "push": false,
     "screen": "years17"
    },
    {
     "who": "anchor",
     "text": "Cuban pianist Alfredo Rodriguez plays Saturday. And Armenian pianist Tigran Hamasyan closes the festival on Sunday.",
     "audio": "audio/v1/ep05_026.mp3",
     "shot": "k_screen",
     "cam_id": "screen_anchor",
     "push": false,
     "screen": [
      "rodriguez",
      "hamasyan"
     ]
    },
    {
     "who": "panel",
     "text": "Closing on a piano. Smooth. Now, how do I get to a turtle island?",
     "audio": "audio/v1/ep05_027.mp3",
     "shot": "k_screen",
     "cam_id": "screen_panel",
     "side": "left",
     "push": false,
     "screen": "hamasyan"
    },
    {
     "who": "anchor",
     "text": "The ITX train from Yongsan to Gapyeong takes about fifty-five minutes. Then it's a twenty-minute walk from the station, or a shuttle bus.",
     "audio": "audio/v1/ep05_028.mp3",
     "shot": "k_screen",
     "cam_id": "screen_anchor",
     "push": false,
     "screen": "itx"
    },
    {
     "who": "guest",
     "text": "I've walked that route. ...On a map.",
     "audio": "audio/v1/ep05_029.mp3",
     "shot": "k_screen",
     "cam_id": "screen_guest",
     "push": false,
     "screen": "itx"
    },
    {
     "who": "anchor",
     "text": "Tickets are sold through Yes24. Kids in elementary school and younger get in free. Middle and high schoolers get half off.",
     "audio": "audio/v1/ep05_030.mp3",
     "shot": "k_screen",
     "cam_id": "screen_anchor",
     "push": false,
     "screen": "kids"
    },
    {
     "who": "panel",
     "text": "And it lands on the Hangul Day long weekend. Everyone's bringing a blanket and a snack.",
     "audio": "audio/v1/ep05_031.mp3",
     "shot": "cam",
     "cam": [
      960,
      500,
      1.1
     ],
     "ease": 0.14,
     "cam_id": "two",
     "push": false
    },
    {
     "who": "anchor",
     "text": "The whole festival is outdoors, with seating on the grass. It's mid-October, so the leaves are at their peak.",
     "audio": "audio/v1/ep05_032.mp3",
     "shot": "k_screen",
     "cam_id": "screen_anchor",
     "push": false,
     "screen": "jarasum_autumn"
    },
    {
     "who": "panel",
     "text": "Blanket, snacks, a Grammy winner, a turtle island. Ten out of ten weekend.",
     "audio": "audio/v1/ep05_033.mp3",
     "shot": "k_screen",
     "cam_id": "screen_panel",
     "side": "left",
     "push": false,
     "screen": "jarasum_autumn"
    }
   ]
  },
